# Code hygiene and file layout

This is HTML + Tailwind (Vite), not React. Do not split the homepage into components “for cleanliness.”

## Live pages

- Home markup: `index.html`
- About markup: `about.html`
- Services markup: `services.html` (accordion in `src/services.js`)
- Straight-Shaft service markup: `services/straight-shaft-pier-drilling.html` (quote form in `src/quote-form.js`)
- Contact markup: `contact.html` (quote form in `src/quote-form.js`, FAQ in `src/contact.js`)
- Careers markup: `careers.html` (apply form in `src/quote-form.js`, FAQ in `src/contact.js`)
- Shared styles: `src/style.css` (tokens, header, hero overlay, marquee, utilities used in more than one section)
- Shared behavior: `src/main.js` (menu, header solid state, marquee, Services dropdown)
- Assets: `public/assets/`

## When inner pages are approved

One HTML file per page. Root files for Home, About, and the Services hub; individual services live under `services/` (`services/straight-shaft-pier-drilling.html`). Register each file in `vite.config.js` `build.rollupOptions.input` or the production/GitHub Pages build will omit it. Reuse header/footer markup and `src/main.js` / `src/style.css`. Add a page JS file (and import it only from that page) only if that page needs unique behavior. Do not start a `pages/` or `components/` tree unless asked.

## Always

- Delete unused CSS, JS, classes, comments, and assets when a change replaces them. Do not leave the old path “just in case.”
- Prefer editing the existing pattern over adding a second one. Two overlay systems (hero vs `.dark-pattern`) stay separate until the designer asks to unify them.
- Hero padding/height stay in `.hero-inner` in CSS. Do not mix `md:pt-*` with `lg:py-*` on that box.
- Update `.cursor/rules` and `figma-homepage-updates` when frame IDs, hero overlay, or page scope change.
